571
00:32:35,001 --> 00:32:39,540
To make ceramic armor from boron carbide, manufacturers use a system that's known as

572
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:40,540
hot pressing.

573
00:32:40,541 --> 00:32:45,160
It's commonly dry pressed using high tonnage presses to form the initial ceramic shape

574
00:32:45,161 --> 00:32:48,380
of the armor that you want.

575
00:32:48,381 --> 00:32:55,860
The material is then put in a non-oxygen atmosphere first, heated up in temperatures that can be

576
00:32:55,861 --> 00:32:57,660
in excess of 3,900 degrees Fahrenheit.

577
00:32:58,420 --> 00:33:01,520
That pressure's up to 1,000, 2,000 psi.

578
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:05,280
And you wind up with a hard, granular material

579
00:33:05,281 --> 00:33:07,700
where the grains are distinctly bonded together

580
00:33:07,701 --> 00:33:09,080
with no cracks.

581
00:33:09,180 --> 00:33:10,180
It's one solid material.

582
00:33:11,700 --> 00:33:14,100
Even though boron carbide ceramic armor

583
00:33:14,101 --> 00:33:15,140
is extremely hard,

584
00:33:15,840 --> 00:33:17,260
bullets don't just bounce off it

